# =============================================================================
#  Where settings live (D-37 - no GitHub Actions, no GitHub Secrets)
# =============================================================================
#  test.env.example -> .env.test.local   TEST project (Local = Test: pnpm dev, test-local.cmd)
#                      created automatically by test-local.cmd (user-only permissions) - fill it in Notepad
#  prod.env.example -> .env.prod.local   PRODUCTION deploy (deploy.cmd) - optional:  node scripts\env-file.mjs prod
#  environments.json                               public production values (ref, URL, publishable key)
#  `pnpm exec supabase login` / `pnpm exec wrangler login`   CLI logins, stored in your Windows profile
#
#  Edge Function secrets are set PER PROJECT in the Supabase dashboard
#  (Edge Functions -> Secrets), never in a file:
#    SB_SECRET_KEY            sb_secret_... of THAT project (key named "edge-functions")
#    SB_PUBLISHABLE_KEY       sb_publishable_... of THAT project
#    TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN       from @BotFather (TEST project: a separate test bot, or leave unset)
#    TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME    Oneteam_app_bot (PROD) / your test bot (TEST)
#    TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET  random 32+ chars, different per project
#    CRON_SECRET              random 32+ chars, different per project
#    ALLOWED_ORIGINS          PROD: https://oneteam.bizdemo.app    TEST: http://localhost:5173
#    AUTH_EMAIL_DOMAIN        optional (default users.bizdemo.app)
#  Random value:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
